  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_022 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.6776, F1=0.6464), which clearly outperforms all other tested configurations. The scvi_n200 RNA encoder is the strongest (0.6776 vs 0.6390 for pca_n2000 vs 0.5251 for scgpt under identical settings), and avgpool+weighted fusion is consistently superior. The key untested variable for the best configuration is the image encoder: with pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l was nearly tied with resnet50 (0.6352 vs 0.6390), but with the much stronger scvi_n200 RNA encoder, the image modality's contribution may shift. config_042 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the direct, minimal-change extension of the best configuration, testing whether a more powerful pretrained image encoder can push accuracy above 0.6776. With only 3 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest direction with a single high-impact variable change is the most budget-efficient choice."
}

